course: dictionary
lesson: 1012
title: Boneless: no bones at all
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bone is the hard part inside a body. The ending -less means "without", so boneless means without bones. Break the word into parts to work out what it means.
explain: «An elephant has 1 trunk, its nose and upper lip joined into one boneless tube with tens of thousands of muscle bundles.» The trunk has no bones, but it is not weak. It is full of muscle, which is why it can curl, lift and suck up water.
explain: In cooking, boneless chicken has had its bones taken out, so it is easy to eat. Informally, a child who goes boneless goes limp and floppy, as if they have no strength to hold themselves up.
fact: Boneless means having no bones, or with the bones taken out.
fact: The ending -less means "without", so boneless means "without bones".
fact: «Boneless» can describe meat or fish with the bones removed, such as chicken fillets.
fact: Some animals, like jellyfish and worms, have no bones at all.
fact: Informally, «boneless» can mean weak and floppy, as if without bones.
exercise: «Mum bought boneless chicken fillets for tea.» What does boneless mean here? | Cooked in a pan | *Without bones | With very big bones | Covered in sauce
exercise: Ella says the elephant's trunk is «boneless». What does that tell you? | It is weak and cannot move at all | *It has no bones, but it is full of muscle | It has bones all the way through | It is made of wood
exercise: Which ending in boneless means "without"? | -ed | -ly | -ful | *-less
test: «After the game, Sam went boneless on the sofa, too tired to move.» What does boneless mean here? | *Weak and floppy, as if without bones | Having no bones in the body | Cold and wet | Very clean and tidy
test: Which animals have no bones at all? | Horses and cows | Birds and fish | Cats and dogs | *Jellyfish and worms
exam: Jayden says boneless only means "without bones", but his friend says it can also mean floppy. Who is right? | The friend, because boneless has no real meaning | Jayden, because informal words are never in dictionaries | Neither, because boneless is a made-up word | *Both are right, because boneless has a literal meaning and an informal one
